title: 'C-c r n c : skg-diffView-goto-next-change'
pid: 33332e6d-17c9-4449-b04a-bd1b36fe5997
body: |2-
  Moves point to the next headline with change facts after point: a headline whose
  metadata carries a '(leaves ...)' change fact, the server's count of the
  changes it names. It skips a ☮ occurrence (not a ghost) standing directly in a folder
  labelled "... (other files)" (its other containers, mentioners or
  hiders changed), and one standing in the forks folder born only of
  forking the viewparent ('(birth (forks out 2))'): that member records
  the relationship in its own file, and its change is drawn, and
  visited, where its node stands editable. C-c r n C visits those too.
  Point lands at the start of the headline's line.
  It does not wrap: past the last one it says "No further
  change" and leaves point, or, when only skipped ones are left, "No
  further change but ☮ ones in "(other files)" folders; C-c r n C visits
  them". It works in any skg buffer; outside the
  diff view no headline names a change, so it finds none.
  In a diff view extended to every change (C-c r u), it reaches every
  change. In one not extended, a node shown only as such a ☮ member has
  its change shown only there, and only C-c r n C reaches it; the
  processed summary counts such changes as not editable in this view.
